SUMMARY:Page Turners Club
DESCRIPTION:Page Turners Club is a fun and engaging summer reading program 
 for rising 2nd and 3rd graders. Join us every Tuesday and Thursday this 
 summer as we explore exciting stories\, build reading confidence\, and 
 discover the joy of books through read-alouds\, activities\, games\, and 
 prizes. Whether your child already loves reading or is just beginning their 
 reading journey\, Page Turners Club is a welcoming space to grow 
 imagination\, friendship\, and a lifelong love of reading.\n\nSnacks will 
 be provided!\n\nRegistration is required! \n
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Side 2\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalia Lucena-Trujillo":MAILTO:nltrujillo@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16796370
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16796370
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260707T150000Z
DTEND:20260707T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260707T000000Z
SUMMARY:Explore Lost Worlds with Mad Science!
DESCRIPTION:Mad Science presents their summer reading show\, Explore Lost 
 Worlds: The Science of Archaeology\, Paleontology\, & Dinosaurs! \n\nOpen a 
 book and reveal a hidden treasure\, from stories to new knowledge! Our Mad 
 Science program sets explorers on an expedition across the ages. They will 
 practice techniques for uncovering the secrets of forgotten worlds and 
 search out creatures long lost in history. There are so many clues that 
 will lead to a great story!\n\nThis program can accommodate up to 55 kids 
 ages 5-11. Please register below!
LOCATION:Bragtown Branch Library (3200 Dearborn Dr)
ORGANIZER;CN="Melanie Jimenez":MAILTO:mrjimenez@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Friends of the Durham Library, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16231489
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16231489
END:VEVENT
