SUMMARY:Summer Learning Bag Giveaway
DESCRIPTION:\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr 
 th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    
 background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\n\n\n\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n  
   color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid 
 #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\nJoin us in the 
 Main Library's Children Programming Room every Tuesday in July (while 
 supplies last) for a special program dedicated to supporting elementary 
 students and their families all summer long. Thanks to a generous grant 
 from the Durham Library Foundation\, the Durham County Library will be 
 distributing Summer Learning Bags designed to help students in grades K-5 
 avoid the “summer slide\,” a time when many children lose progress in 
 reading and math skills.\n\nEach Summer Learning Bag is thoughtfully 
 assembled and filled with fun\, engaging materials including hands-on 
 activities\, math games\, sensory items\, school supplies\, and books to 
 inspire a love of reading throughout the summer months.\n\nBag Giveaway 
 Times:\n\n\n	Morning: 11:00 AM - 12:00 PM\n	Afternoon: 2:00 PM - 3:00 
 PM\n\n\nTo ensure equal access\, children must be present to pick up their 
 Summer Learning Bag. Bags are distributed one per child based on their 
 rising grade level and are available on a first-come\, first-served basis 
 while supplies last.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Maria Ramirez-Heuser":MAILTO:mrheuser@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement, Literacy, Low Sensory Stimulation
