DTEND:20260714T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260714T000000Z
SUMMARY:POSTPONED - Food Fibs: Agriculture Misinformation with Cooperative Extension
DESCRIPTION:Due to scheduling changes\, this event with Coopertive 
 Extension is now POSTPONED to Tuesday\, September 1st from 6-7:30pm. Please 
 register for the September 1st date here - 
 https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17186355\n\nThank you!\n\nEver 
 feel confused about information and misinformation surroudning agriculture 
 and nutrition? Join us for a program and discussion about misinformation 
 and agriculture! This presentation will discuss common misconceptions and 
 myths associated with agriculture in North Carolina and the country as a 
 whole. Lead by agents from the North Carolina Cooperative Extension in 
 Durham\, this program will have a presenation for the first portion of the 
 program time\, followed by Q&A and more discussion. Feel free to bring 
 questions and participate in discussion together.\n\nRegistration is 
 required. The content of this program will be geared towards adults and 
 teens.\n\nThis event will take place in the Innovation Lab on third floor 
 of Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701).\n\nNote: If you 
 have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us 
 at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least 3 
 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible!
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Durham, STEAM
