SUMMARY:Maintenance Fundamentals with Home Repair Lab
DESCRIPTION:Join Chris and Mindy Meyers from Home Repair Lab to learn about 
 maintenance fundamentals! This lecture-focused class will help you 
 understand how your home operates\, give you knowledge to interact with 
 service providers\, and be your own advocate. Relevant for homeowners\, 
 first time home buyers\, and renters. The first hour will be lecture\, 
 followed by Q&A.\n\nMore detailed class description:\n\nMaintenance 
 Fundamentals helps you organize and schedule tasks that extend and improve 
 the safety and life of your home. Experience a year in the life of a 
 homeowner using our seasonal maintenance checklist. Each season elements of 
 your home should be inspected to determine the current state of condition\, 
 good\, repair or replace. We provide specific examples of where to look\, 
 what to look for and how to determine condition. Additionally\, we detail 
 actions homeowners need to perform to maintain a safe\, healthy and 
 comfortable home. All participants receive a copy of our maintenance 
 checklist to keep. \n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Sensory Friendly, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-15947173
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15947173
