SUMMARY:Guest Author: Brenda K. Williamson
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special story time with author Dr. Brenda K. 
 Williamson\, where she’ll be presenting her book: Artena: “What’s 
 Inside of You?”\n\n\nDr. Brenda K. Williamson has more than 35 years of 
 experience in the field of education\, ranging from serving as a 
 kindergarten teacher to working as an assistant and associate professor. 
 She is the founder of Brenda’s Educational Consultant Services (BECS)\, 
 which provides professional development training at the local\, state\, 
 national\, and international levels on a wide range of topics.\n\nShe is 
 the lead founder of the NCAEYC Equity in Early Childhood Education Circle 
 Sessions\, designed to facilitate courageous conversations and promote 
 equitable practices. In 2022\, she founded Black Women Educators of NC to 
 inspire\, uplift\, and support Black women educators through leadership 
 development\, networking\, and research.
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Side 2\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalia Lucena-Trujillo":MAILTO:nltrujillo@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Story Time
