SUMMARY:Bull City Jazz Listening
DESCRIPTION:Slide on in and catch the groove! Our Jazz Listening Series in 
 collaboration with the legendary North Carolina Central University Jazz 
 Studies Program is back!  We’re bringing the soul\, the swing\, the 
 stories\, and the shine of Black musical brilliance right into the historic 
 Stanford L. Warren Library.\n\nEach session is a fun\, 
 come‑as‑you‑are listening hangout where we spin classic cuts\, 
 uncover hidden gems\, and spotlight the Black innovators who shaped jazz 
 from the Carolinas to the world. With insight and vibes straight from 
 NCCU’s award‑winning faculty\, students\, and alumni\, and local jazz 
 afficionados you’ll hear the music—and the culture—through the ears 
 of real jazz insiders.\n\nExpect laughter\, lively conversation\, and 
 plenty of “Wait\, who was THAT?” moments as we celebrate the rhythms\, 
 roots\, and rich traditions of African American jazz.\n\nPull up\, tap in\, 
 and let’s groove together. The music is fire\, the company is warm\, and 
 the culture is ours to celebrate.
LOCATION:SLW Meeting Room - Full Room\, Stanford L. Warren Branch Library (1201 Fayetteville St)
