BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260718T190000Z
DTEND:20260718T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260718T000000Z
SUMMARY:Jurassic Park: Floats & Films
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Summer Reading with a screening of Jurassic Park. 
 While you watch\, cool down with a root beer float!\n\nIn Jurassic Park\, 
 "Paleontologists Alan Grant (Sam Neill) and Ellie Sattler (Laura Dern) and 
 mathematician Ian Malcolm (Jeff Goldblum) are among a select group chosen 
 to tour an island theme park populated by dinosaurs created from 
 prehistoric DNA. While the park's mastermind\, billionaire John Hammond 
 (Richard Attenborough)\, assures everyone that the facility is safe\, they 
 find out otherwise when various ferocious predators break free and go on 
 the hunt."\n\nRated: PG-13\n\nRun time: 2 hours 2 minutes\n\nThe movie will 
 be shown with closed captions. Root beer floats and popcorn will be 
 provided. All ages are encouraged to attend. Registration is appreciated 
 but not required.\n\nQuestions? Contact Mara (she/her): 
 mplantholt@dconc.gov.\n\n2026 Summer Reading is made possible thanks to the 
 generous support of the Durham Library Foundation and the Friends of the 
 Durham Library.
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Movie, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16217465
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16217465
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260718T200000Z
DTEND:20260718T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260718T000000Z
SUMMARY:Durham County Library @ The Carolina Blaze Game!
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that Durham is home to a Women's Professional 
 Softball Team? The Carolina Blaze were established in 2025 as one of the 
 four original teams in the Athletes Unlimited Softball League (AUSL) - a 
 professional softball league in the United States.\n\nDurham County Library 
 will be at the game on Saturday\, July 18th at Smith Family Stadium. Come 
 visit the Bookmobile while cheering on the Blaze! First pitch is at 4:00pm 
 with the gates opening at 2:30pm.\n\nTickets for the game can be purchased 
 at the Carolina Blaze's website. Use Promo Code: AUSL-LIBRARY for 10% 
 off.\n\nSmith Family Stadium\n\n4 Brodie Gym Dr\, Durham\, NC 
 27705\n\nLocated in Duke East Campus
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Sara Gibson":MAILTO:sgibson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Announcements, Bookmobile, Community Engagement
UID:LibCal-14288-16911107
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16911107
