BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260720T221500Z
DTEND:20260720T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260720T000000Z
SUMMARY:Read it Again and Again: How do Picture Books Work?
DESCRIPTION:Join Jennifer Stone\, PhD\, CCC-SLP as she teaches us how 
 picture books work and what are the best ways use them.\n\nAny adult 
 (parents\, caregivers\, teachers\, etc.) who wants to learn more about 
 picture books and how they work is welcome to register. We hope to provide 
 a fun and engaging space to learn how to increase critical literacy for 
 ourselves and the children we read with. As a group\, we will read a 
 picture book and then discuss theoretical frameworks that can be used for 
 analysis. Then we'll choose a different lens and read the book again to see 
 what we discover! Dr. Stone will draw upon multiple sources including 
 Poetry Unbound\, Five in a Row\, and modern pedagogical texts including 
 "Media Literacy for Young Children: Teaching Beyond the Screen Time 
 Debates". This will be an interactive workshop\, and patrons are invited to 
 share feelings\, observations\, ideas\, and ask questions. We welcome you 
 all for a night of learning and sharing!\n\n \n\n \n\nJennifer Stone\, 
 PhD\, CCC-SLP\n\nJennifer Stone lives in South Durham and owns Stone Circle 
 Speech Therapy and Parent Coaching. She has specialized in early 
 intervention\, parent coaching\, and literacy for over 30 years. Her work 
 has taken her to hundreds of homes and she loves learning about parents' 
 resourcefulness and creativity. In addition to therapy and coaching\, Dr. 
 Stone is a researcher\, and her doctoral research focused on Dolly Parton's 
 Imagination Library and social power systems. She sees picture books as 
 literary works that can transform our understanding and our culture. Dr. 
 Stone loves sharing and learning about them with others who appreciate them 
 as art. In addition to her work\, Stone is a mom of two adults\, whom she 
 homeschooled before they graduated from North Carolina School of Science 
 and Math and NC universities. She loves reading\, dancing\, traveling\, and 
 being in nature. \n\n
LOCATION:South Meeting Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaris T.":MAILTO:amaristorres@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Community Engagement, Homeschool, Humanities, Literacy, Low Sensory Stimulation, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16860357
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16860357
END:VEVENT
