SUMMARY:Homeschool Learning Lab: Fossil Dig
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a prehistoric plunge into ancient seas! Recommended 
 for children ages 5 and up\, this hands-on experience invites young 
 paleontologists to explore mini fossil dig sites and uncover real marine 
 fossils\, such as shark teeth and coral. During the dig\, participants can 
 take a closer look at their discoveries using a microscope.\n\nThis program 
 will be held at North Regional Library Thursday\, July 23\, 2026\, at 
 10a.m. The address is 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712.   \n\nThis event 
 will be held outside\, weather permitting\, so please dress accordingly. 
 \n\nHomeschool Learning Lab meets weekly year-round. In the summer\, we ask 
 for registration in order to help with program prep. Please register each 
 child attending. \n\nIf you have any questions\, accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact Molly at mschaefer@dconc.gov.  We ask 
 that all requests be made at least three (3) business days prior to the 
 event to ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible!
LOCATION:North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Homeschool, Summer Reading
