SUMMARY:Diamond Dinos!
DESCRIPTION:Unearth a Story with this Summer Reading program for adults! 
 \n\nDo you love diamond painting? Do you also love dinosaurs? Would you 
 love to learn more about dinosaurs while diamond painting dinosaurs? If 
 so\, you're in luck! Join us to watch the North Carolina Museum of 
 Science's recording of "Lunchtime Discovery Series: The End of the World\, 
 an Introduction to the End-Permian Mass Extinction" while we diamond paint 
 dinosaur figurines! \n\nAll supplies\, including coffee and tea\, will be 
 provided. \n\nRegistration is required\, as supplies are limited. We will 
 meet in the large meeting room of the North Regional Library\, 221 Milton 
 Rd.
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Desiree Peterson":MAILTO:dpeterson@dconc.gov
