DTSTART:20260725T170000Z
DTEND:20260725T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260725T000000Z
SUMMARY:Page & Pen Writing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:\n\nGrab your notebook and a pen\, and let's write! The Page & 
 Pen Writing Workshop meets roughly every six weeks and is open to anyone 
 who wants to improve their creative writing skills. Session formats vary 
 and may include writing exercises\, discussion about technique and 
 process\, sharing ideas for organizing work sessions and workspaces\, or 
 exploration of any challenges you may be facing in the struggle to 
 write.\n\nTopic for this session: The Protagonist. Are you working on a 
 project that has a protagonist? What makes a strong and compelling main 
 character? We'll analyze examples from a few short stories and novels and 
 share opinions about what works and what doesn't.\n\n\n\nThis program is 
 open to anyone at any time: drop in once\, attend every session\, or show 
 up every once in a while -- no long-term commitment is required. Space is 
 often limited\, so please register in advance.\n\nContact Bob with any 
 questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
