SUMMARY:Day 1 – Agricultural Business\, Marketing\, Finance & Entrepreneurship
DESCRIPTION:Free NC A&T & PHIRST® workshop series. Attend 1 day\, multiple 
 days\, or all 4: business\, agriculture\, technology & future 
 farming.\n\nPHIRST® PovertyZero™ Farms & Food Workshop Series with NC 
 A&T\n\nJoin North Carolina A&T State University and PHIRST® for a free 
 four-day workshop series focused on certification pathways\, sustainable 
 agriculture\, practical skills\, enterprise development\, and applied 
 learning. Participants may attend one day\, multiple days\, or the full 
 four-day series.\n\nThe workshop series is designed for farmers\, future 
 farmers\, backyard growers\, entrepreneurs\, educators\, students\, and 
 community leaders seeking practical knowledge\, certification 
 opportunities\, hands-on experience\, and sustainable enterprise 
 strategies.\n\nDAY 1 – AGRICULTURAL BUSINESS\, MARKETING\, FINANCE & 
 ENTREPRENEURSHIP\nParticipants explore direct marketing strategies\, niche 
 farming opportunities\, transportation and storage of agricultural 
 products\, business planning\, value-added enterprises\, financial 
 planning\, cash flow\, recordkeeping\, heirs' property\, business 
 structures\, tax preparation\, and entrepreneurship. This day focuses on 
 building profitable and sustainable agricultural enterprises.\n\nWHAT YOU 
 WILL GAIN\n Practical agricultural knowledge and skills\n Sustainable 
 farming and enterprise strategies\n Certification opportunities through NC 
 A&T OPPE pathways\n Exposure to innovative technologies and systems\n 
 Networking with agricultural professionals\, educators\, entrepreneurs\, 
 and community leaders\n Real-world examples of scalable agricultural 
 enterprises\n\nAttendance is free\, but registration is required.\nSeating 
 is limited to 24 participants per day. \n\nAttend one day\, multiple days\, 
 or the entire four-day series.\n\nLearn. Grow. Innovate. Build 
 Sustainably.\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the 
 North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind 
 the apartments directly across the street from the library. Parking at the 
 garage is free. Please bring your parking ticket to a service point for 
 validation.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17111380
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17111380
END:VEVENT
